  "goodToKnow": "Die Möwe is a seagull, a symbol of the North Sea and Baltic coast. At resorts, Möwen are notorious for snatching Fischbrötchen and ice cream from tourists, and feeding them is banned in many places. Christian Morgenstern's humorous poem Möwenlied plays with the name. Chekhov's play The Seagull is Die Möwe in German. Plural: die Möwen."
